    {
      "image": "videos/04-open-loops/3.jpg",
      "seconds": 20.29,
      "text": "An unfinished task is a browser tab your mind refuses to close. It costs memory to hold it open, so your brain keeps pushing it back into view. Every cliffhanger, every unread notification, every argument you walked away from runs on this. Which means attention is not something you give. It is something that gets taken, by whatever you left open.",
      "delivery": {
        "rate": 8,
        "pitch": -1
      },
      "clips": [
